  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a twenty-song set at the Bowery Ballroom in New York on October 1, 2007 [1]. This audience recording, captured by bluesmer, runs for seventy-seven minutes and includes the full lineup [1]. The set features several rare tracks, such as “Tulsa Imperative,” which had not been played in over nine years, and “Pure Milk,” a similar bustout [1]. Other less common songs include “How to Embrace a Swamp Creature,” “Half Dead,” and “Going to Queens” [1]. The performance also covers well-known material like “Cheshire County,” “Wild Sage,” and “Dilaudid” [1]. This is the only available recording of the event, rated five out of five by two listeners [1]. One reviewer, rubinmoon, noted in 2020 that they listen to this specific recording frequently despite its age [2]. Another listener, nigelewan, mentioned in 2024 that they have enjoyed a copy of this show since 2007, describing it as an incredible time capsule of the band as a full-time duo [3]. The recording documents the band’s sound during this period, offering a complete view of their live performance [1][3].",
